// Minor Illusion, sound mode. Companion to minor_illusion_image.ron --
// authored so the school's data is complete, but NOT wired into
// compendium.ron (that entry's `ability` field points at the image RON
// instead; see that file's own comment for why only one specifier can win).
//
// Scope note: this mode is supposed to conjure a fleeting sound at the
// target point rather than an image. The engine's only sound-emission path,
// `SoundEvent`/`SoundKind` (`server/src/events/interaction.rs`), is an
// AI-stimulus system consumed by a `BehaviorTree` node reading an `Agent` --
// it is not a player-audible SFX trigger. Phantasms are `with_agent: false`
// by design (see `common/src/comp/phantom_illusion.rs`: giving one an
// `Agent` to make it "hearable" would reintroduce the AI surface the
// mechanism exists to avoid), so that path is not reachable here without new
// Rust. No data-only field exists on `SummonInfo::Npc` (or anywhere else) to
// emit a `SoundEvent`/audible cue from a spell cast. This RON therefore ships
// the same phantasm shape as the image mode -- an unkillable, un-AI'd,
// short-lived decoy point -- without literal audio; wiring in real sound
// would need a small new field on `SummonInfo::Npc` plus a system to act on
// it, deliberately left for a future pass rather than invented here.
BasicSummon(
    buildup_duration: 0.3,
    cast_duration: 0.1,
    recover_duration: 0.3,
    summon_info: Npc(
        summoned_amount: 1,
        summon_distance: (1.0, 2.0),
        body: Object(Coconut),
        scale: None,
        has_health: false,
        use_npc_name: false,
        loadout_config: None,
        skillset_config: None,
        // Much shorter than the image mode: this represents a single brief
        // sound (a snap, a bark, footsteps), not a sustained decoy.
        duration: Some((
            secs: 10,
            nanos: 0,
        )),
        alignment: Some(Passive),
        with_agent: false,
        incorporeal: true,
        phantom_illusion: true,
        delete_after_expiry: true,
    ),
)
